---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ReviewedByCard from "../../components/ReviewedByCard.astro";
import { TRUST_PROFILES } from "../../config/trust";

const title = "Extra Payment Prepayment Penalty Checklist";
const description =
  "Prepayment penalty checklist for extra mortgage payments: confirm lender rules before accelerating payoff. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-06-26";
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/guides/extra-payment-prepayment-penalty-checklist"
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  robots="noindex, follow"
  authorProfile={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
  reviewProfiles={[TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview, TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview]}
>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Prepayment penalty</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Prepayment penalty checklist for extra payments</h1>
    <p>
      Some loans charge prepayment penalties or limit how extra payments are applied. Use this checklist to confirm rules before you
      accelerate payoff.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/extra-mortgage-payments">Extra payment guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ReviewedByCard
    writtenBy={TRUST_PROFILES.siteOwner}
    reviewedBy={TRUST_PROFILES.editorialReview}
    secondaryReview={TRUST_PROFILES.methodologyReview}
    reviewScope="Penalty-window verification, note-review framing, and routing between extra-payment modeling and narrower loan-note checks."
    reviewedOn={lastUpdated}
  />

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How this page fits the extra-payment workflow</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Use this support page for one narrow note-review question: does the loan still have a prepayment penalty or payout rule that can change the payoff math?
      It is not the main entry point for the payoff strategy. If you still need the bigger decision about whether to prepay, return to the
      <a href="/guides/extra-mortgage-payments"> main extra payment guide</a> and then use this page only after the loan-note question becomes specific.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Read the note for prepayment penalty terms.</li>
      <li>Check if penalties apply only in the first few years.</li>
      <li>Ask the servicer how extra payments are applied (principal-only vs paid ahead).</li>
      <li>Confirm any caps on extra payment amounts.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Prepayment penalty inputs to confirm</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Penalty window dates and remaining months.</li>
      <li>Penalty formula (percent vs months of interest).</li>
      <li>Cap on extra payment amounts.</li>
      <li>Whether penalties apply to partial prepayments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Assuming all loans allow unlimited prepayments.</li>
      <li>Sending extra without a principal-only instruction.</li>
      <li>Ignoring a penalty window that is still active.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Where to confirm penalties</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Promissory note or loan agreement.</li>
      <li>Closing Disclosure or Loan Estimate.</li>
      <li>Servicer FAQ or payment portal.</li>
      <li>Direct confirmation from the servicer.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Questions for the servicer</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Does the penalty apply to partial prepayments or only full payoff?</li>
      <li>Is there a declining schedule by year or balance?</li>
      <li>How is the fee calculated (percent vs months of interest)?</li>
      <li>Is advance notice or a specific form required?</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Remaining balance and months left in any penalty window.</li>
      <li>Penalty formula and any caps or thresholds.</li>
      <li>Extra payment amount you plan to apply now.</li>
      <li>Expected refinance or sale timing.</li>
      <li>Alternative uses for the cash (higher-rate debt or reserves).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Penalty math quick check</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Estimate the fee in dollars using the stated formula.</li>
      <li>Compare the fee to interest saved over your horizon.</li>
      <li>Check if the fee expires soon and whether waiting helps.</li>
      <li>Document the calculation for your records.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Timing and notice</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ask if a payoff quote is required for the exact payment date.</li>
      <li>Confirm how long the quote is valid and how to request a refresh.</li>
      <li>Plan mailing or processing time so the payment posts on schedule.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Extra payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/principal-only-extra-payments">Principal-only extra payments</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/mortgage-recast-vs-extra-payments">Recast vs extra payments</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/extra-payment-calculator">Model extra payments</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/extra-mortgage-payments">Main extra payment guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/mortgage-payoff">Mortgage payoff topic hub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-06-26</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
